# =============================================================================
# ReserveToday — fe-portal env (Next.js)
# =============================================================================

# ---- Backend [required] ------------------------------------------------------
# Where this fe-portal calls for /api/v1/portal/* — must match where the
# `be` server is listening.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# ---- Tenant resolution [required] --------------------------------------------
# Everything after the tenant slug. The slug is the hostname minus this suffix,
# and that is the ONLY rule — local, staging and production differ solely in
# this value, so a Host-parsing bug cannot appear in production alone.
#
#   local        portal.localhost:3001        -> acme.portal.localhost:3001
#   staging      portal.dev.reservetoday.app  -> acme.portal.dev.reservetoday.app
#   production   portal.reservetoday.app      -> acme.portal.reservetoday.app
#
# The `portal.` label stays in the local value even though port 3001 already
# separates the apps: it makes this app exercise the same two-label strip it
# runs in production. `*.localhost` (multi-level included) resolves to loopback
# in Chrome, Edge and Firefox with no hosts-file entry. Being a NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# var, it must ALSO be set in the Vercel dashboard (Production and Preview) —
# see docs/md/deployment.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ROOT_DOMAIN=portal.localhost:3001

# ---- Clerk: staff app [required] ---------------------------------------------
# These are the SAME values you set on the backend's CLERK_STAFF_* keys —
# one Clerk application is shared between fe-portal and `be`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=

# ---- Clerk: super portal app [optional] --------------------------------------
# A THIRD Clerk application, used ONLY on `admin.portal.<root domain>`. These are
# the same values you set on the backend's CLERK_PLATFORM_* keys.
#
# Why an application and not a setting: Clerk's session is the `__client` cookie,
# scoped to the instance's own Frontend API host (`Domain=clerk.portal.…`,
# HttpOnly). One Clerk application serving two hostnames is therefore one
# signed-in person across both — sign in at `admin.portal.…` and every
# `{slug}.portal.…` is already signed in as that account. A second application
# means a second Frontend API host, so a second `__client`, so two sessions.
#
# All THREE below or none — the two keys and CLERK_ENCRYPTION_KEY. A partial
# configuration mints tokens with one instance and verifies them with another.
# Blank leaves the pre-existing shared-session behaviour, still gated at the API
# by the backend's PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS.
#
# Read in `src/lib/clerk-keys.ts` and applied in two places that must agree —
# `<ClerkProvider publishableKey>` in `src/app/layout.tsx` (the browser) and the
# `clerkMiddleware` options callback in `src/proxy.ts` (the server).
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` must ALSO be set in the Vercel dashboard (Production and
# Preview) — see docs/md/deployment.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PLATFORM_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_PLATFORM_SECRET_KEY=

# Required by Clerk WHENEVER `secretKey` is passed to clerkMiddleware() at
# request time, which `src/proxy.ts` does on the super portal's hostname. Clerk
# encrypts the dynamic keys into the request (AES) before the server helpers
# read them back, and throws when a secret arrives without this — on the
# NextResponse.next() path, so every request including /login. That is why
# clerk-keys.ts counts it as part of the platform configuration rather than
# treating it as optional: leaving it blank falls back to the shared session
# instead of 500ing the super portal. Ideally a 32-byte random value:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
CLERK_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Note: Clerk routing URLs (sign-in / sign-up / redirects) are HARDCODED as
# props on <ClerkProvider> in src/app/layout.tsx — they don't belong in env
# because they're tied to this codebase's route structure.

# ---- Error monitoring (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Set in Vercel Preview/Production to enable Sentry in deployed builds.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
